[al:新概念英语（三）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Fifty Pence Worth of Trouble]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.44]Lesson 15 | 第15课
[00:02.65]Fifty pence worth of trouble | 50便士的麻烦
[00:10.16]Did George get anything for his fifty pence? What? | 乔治的50便士换来了什么？
[00:16.65]Children always appreciate small gifts of money. | 孩子们总是把得到的一小笔钱看得很重。
[00:20.60]Mum or dad, of course, provides a regular supply of pocket money, but uncles and aunts are always a source of extra income. | 当然，爸爸妈妈会经常给零花钱，但叔叔舅舅们也是额外收入的来源。
[00:30.99]With some children, small sums go a long way. | 对有些孩子来说，小钱能派上大用场。
[00:35.17]If fifty pence pieces are not exchanged for sweets, they rattle for months inside money boxes. | 如果50便士的硬币没有换成糖果，它们便会在储蓄罐里叮当作响好几个月。
[00:43.16]Only very thrifty children manage to fill up a money box. | 只有非常节俭的孩子才能把储蓄罐装满。
[00:48.59]For most of them, fifty pence is a small price to pay for a nice big bar of chocolate. | 对他们大多数人来说，用50便士买一大块好吃的巧克力，花这点钱不算什么。
[00:56.95]My nephew, George, has a money box but it is always empty. | 我的侄子乔治有一个储蓄罐，但总是空空如也。
[01:02.34]Very few of the fifty pence pieces and pound coins I have given him have found their way there. | 我给过他的50便士和1英镑的硬币，很少有存进去的。
[01:10.05]I gave him fifty pence yesterday and advised him to save it. | 昨天我给了他50便士，建议他存起来。
[01:14.63]Instead, he bought himself fifty pence worth of trouble. | 相反，他用这50便士给自己买来了麻烦。
[01:19.56]On his way to the sweet shop, he dropped his fifty pence and it bounced along the pavement and then disappeared down a drain. | 在去糖果店的路上，他的50便士掉了，硬币在人行道上蹦蹦跳跳，随后滚进了阴沟。
[01:29.81]George took off his jacket, | 乔治脱下外套，
[01:32.21]rolled up his sleeves and pushed his right arm through the drain cover. | 挽起袖子，把右胳膊从阴沟盖的孔里伸了进去。
[01:37.54]He could not find his 50 pence piece anywhere, and what is more, he could not get his arm out. | 他怎么也摸不到那枚50便士的硬币，更糟的是，胳膊也抽不出来了。
[01:45.86]A crowd of people gathered round him and a lady rubbed his arm with soap and butter, but George was firmly stuck. | 一群人围在他身边，一位女士用肥皂和黄油擦他的胳膊，但乔治被牢牢地卡住了。
[01:55.35]The fire brigade was called and two fire fighters freed George using a special type of grease. | 消防队被叫来了，两名消防队员用一种特殊的润滑脂把乔治解脱了出来。
[02:02.73]George was not too upset by his experience because the lady who owns the sweet shop heard about his troubles and rewarded him with a large box of chocolates. | 乔治并没有因这段经历而过于烦恼，因为糖果店的女老板听说了他的遭遇，奖给了他一大盒巧克力。
